+# Drone MVP Medium Bag Sample Testing Completed (2026-10-28)
+
+## Summary
+
+IKC Ops has completed the bag sample testing that was the open next step in [[drone-mvp-medium-bag-outer-package-decision]]. The mailed samples — described in the follow-up as the new August 2026 Medium bag, the PRD v26 default, and the guest packaging — fit the **production Pod**. The new Medium is confirmed as the MVP outer package, and no further bag testing is planned before launch.
+
+This closes the "samples still need testing" condition that the 2026-08-12 Slack thread left open. It does not publish a bag SKU, tare, fill line, folded height, orientation or handle/closure rule, and it is not a Zipline test report.
+
+## Detail
+
+### What the follow-up says
+
+On 2026-10-28 Jay relayed Rob Knudson's follow-up, appended by the note owner as an `## Update (2026-10-28)` section of the 2026-08-12 Slack clarification note:
+
+- IKC Ops completed the sample testing.
+- The mailed samples fit the production Pod (not the 3D printed Pod sample used in the August check).
+- The new Medium is confirmed as the MVP outer package.
+- No further bag testing is planned before launch.
+
+### What it closes
+
+| Earlier open item (as of 2026-10-19) | Status after 2026-10-28 |
+| --- | --- |
+| Sample-fit test of mailed bag and guest-packaging samples (2026-08-12 "next step") | Completed; samples fit the production Pod. |
+| Jay's 2026-08-20 interpretation that the mailed samples are the new August Medium, "pending confirmation" | Consistent with the follow-up, which names the mailed sample "the new August 2026 Medium bag". |
+| Whether further bag testing would precede launch | None planned. |
+
+### What it does not establish
+
+- **Dimension identity.** The follow-up treats "the new August 2026 Medium bag" and "the PRD v26 default" as the same bag. The decision record carries two different nominal sizes for the new Medium: `13" × 10" × 13"` from the August 2026 bag specification and `12 × 8.5 × 13 in` from PRD v26. The follow-up does not say which tuple is correct or whether they describe the same SKU. This is unresolved and is surfaced in `## Open` on the citing concept page.
+- Bag SKU, empty-bag tare, maximum fill line, folded height, allowed orientation, handle/closure treatment.
+- A Zipline-side test report or validation detail beyond PRD v26's statement; the completed test described here is the IKC Ops Pod-fit check.
+- Whether "guest packaging" fit was evaluated per configuration or as one representative sample.
+- Any change to the Zipline provider envelope (`338 × 254 × 205 mm / 2495 g`) or to order-specific Zipline Pack evaluation.
+
+### Evidence quality
+
+The evidence is a single relayed attestation (Rob, via Jay) recorded by the note owner. It agrees with PRD v26's reported validation of the new Medium rather than contradicting any current source, so it is absorbed as a confirmation. The one tension it introduces (the dimension identity above) is recorded as open, not resolved.
+
